        "original_id": "ef6ad1fe-b56e-5d13-bb96-9bfd38090e6e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: American League, National League, Major League Baseball\n- Concepts: designated hitter rule, designated hitter (DH), Rule 5.11\n\nFacts:\n- The American League has a notable difference from the National League in its use of the designated hitter rule.\n- In 1973, the American League adopted the designated hitter rule, which is the common name for Major League Baseball Rule 5.11.\n- The designated hitter rule allows a team to use one player, called the designated hitter or DH, to bat in place of the pitcher.",
